---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{#
  layouts/contact.njk
  Renders src/contact.md, top to bottom:

    1. A huge line of greetings that scrolls endlessly across the full
       width of the window. The words come from the "marquee" field in
       contact.md (editable in /admin -> Pages -> Contact). The scrolling
       itself is pure CSS (see .marquee in style.css); a few lines in
       main.js only tune its speed to the width of the text.
    2. The intro text - "content" below, the Markdown body of contact.md.
       The first paragraph is shown bold, the next ones lighter.
    3. "Request a proposal" (email + phone) and "Follow me" (Instagram).

  The page title is kept in the HTML for screen readers and search
  engines but hidden visually, since the nav already shows where you are.
#}

<h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ title }}</h1>

{% if marquee %}
{#
  Decorative, so it is hidden from screen readers. The text appears twice
  (two "groups") so that when the first one has scrolled out of view the
  second is already in its place, and the loop never shows a gap.
#}
<div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="marquee__track">
    <span class="marquee__group">{{ marquee }}</span>
    <span class="marquee__group">{{ marquee }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="contact">

  <div class="contact__text">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>

  <div class="contact__details">
    {% if email or phone %}
    <div class="contact__block">
      <p class="contact__label">Request a proposal</p>
      {% if email %}<a href="mailto:{{ email }}">{{ email }}</a>{% endif %}
      {% if phone %}<a href="tel:{{ phone | replace(' ', '') }}">{{ phone }}</a>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if instagram %}
    <div class="contact__block">
      <p class="contact__label">Follow me</p>
      <a href="{{ instagram }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Instagram</a>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

</div>
